    "lawCode": "Amd §18, Chap 408 of 1999",
    "lawSection": "Mental Hygiene",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6726\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend chapter 408 of the laws of 1999\nconstituting Kendra's law, in relation to extending the expiration\nthereof\n\n PURPOSE OF THE BILL :\n\nTo extend the ability to order assisted outpatient treatment (AOT)\nfrom June 30, 2017, to June 30, 2022.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nThis bill would extend Kendra's Law until June 30, 2022.\n\n STATEMENT IN SUPPORT :\n\nThis law established a statutory framework for court ordered assisted\noutpatient treatment (AOT) which is intended to ensure that\nindividuals with mental illness and a history of hospitalizations or\nviolence participate in community based treatment appropriate to their\nindividual needs. And further provides a process for obtaining court\norders for individuals with mental illness who meet specific criteria\nto receive and engage in outpatient treatment.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nPrevious extenders\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nUndetermined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediate.\n",
